+A leading-flag local component occurrence stores its identity flag before its GUIDs. The primary record index selects the carrier, and the Component occurrence-placement type row (§1.4) registers its record. After the indexed header, the frame stores u32 `0`, an empty LP-ASCII instance name, `u8 1` at offset 19, u32 path count `1` at offset 20, the marked u64 component-record reference at offset 24, two zero bytes, and the u32 path discriminator at offset 35. An attribute list follows: `u8 1` at offset 39 and u32 attribute count at offset 40, then the attributes in the attributed-form encoding. With an empty list, the u16 ordinal prefix is at offset 44, the u32 one-based occurrence ordinal is at offset 46, and the identity flag is at offset 50. Flag `0` stores a row-major orthonormal local-to-container matrix at offset 51, with translation in centimetres. A nonempty list moves every later field by its byte length. The body follows the flag or the matrix: the LP-UTF16 carrier GUID, the LP-UTF16 occurrence GUID, a marked same-segment record reference, one zero byte, `u8 1`, u32 path count `1`, one zero byte, the repeated marked component-record reference, two zero bytes, and a copy of the identity flag. A matrix frame then stores the same matrix a second time. Nine zero bytes, the marker `u8 1`, the u64 owner entity, and two zero bytes close the frame. With an empty attribute list, the identity frame is 251 bytes and the matrix frame is 507 bytes. Flag `1` with ordinal one is the base placement, and flag `0` is the matrix placement. As in the fixed frames, a class-`256` carrier uses the matrix frame only for an ordinal greater than one. A flagless identity frame omits the identity flag after the ordinal: the carrier GUID follows the ordinal directly, and the flag copy `1` in the body is its only identity flag. With an empty attribute list it is 250 bytes. The prefix and body layouts are in [the layout tables](../layouts/f3d.md).
 
 An attributed local component occurrence also permits a typed component reference. Its path discriminator follows the complete reference at offset 75, the attribute marker is at offset 79, and the attribute count is at offset 80. The attribute run starts at offset 84. The repeated definition reference has the same target and inline type as the first. The closing owner reference is typed and carries inline type GUID `904F885E-D859-4755-A7EF-6EBED8732FAD`. The remaining members have the same order and meanings as in the untyped attributed form.
 
